# negative seed.
#
# Scenario: an execution path returns a BARE SCALAR with no world label —
# a value that looks like an answer but hides which world produced it,
# with no disposition, evidence, or cost. Any consumer (CLI, WASM, lab
# lens) could mistake it for the intended meaning: silent success. The
# WorldResultBundle envelope refuses this: a result without its world
# label / method / disposition is a typed refusal (E-WORLD-001..003) and
# never enters a bundle; dispositions (answer/open/refused/fault) are
# first-class, and the bundle id replays deterministically.
#
# expect: E-WORLD-001 - the envelope refuses the naked result with a
# typed refusal naming the missing label; every bundleable execution
# carries world, method, inputs, assumptions, disposition, evidence, and
# cost labels.
use std.kinds.capability

emath custom NakedResult:
    world constructor unlabelled:
        # seeded naked path: the value is returned without evidence
        symbols:
            q: 1
        carrier: Integer
    strategies:
        select: bare-scalar-no-provenance
